# Question: if the scope grows while we build it, how much later do we finish
# than the plan says, and how likely are we to miss the date?
#
# Run it:
#   ubc --scenario delivery/scope-creep
# Change an assumption, for example scope that is kept under control:
#   ubc --set 'growth = 5% to 15%' --scenario delivery/scope-creep
# See which assumption matters most:
#   ubc --sens weeks --scenario delivery/scope-creep
#
# Every "a to b" is a 90% confidence interval.

# Assumptions
initial_scope = 80 to 120         # items in the plan when we commit to the date
growth = 10% to 60%               # scope added before the end; requirements found while building, often 25-50%
throughput = 8 to 12              # items finished a week
deadline = 12                     # weeks until the committed date

# Calculation
scope = initial_scope * (1 + growth)       # items we will really build
planned_weeks = initial_scope / throughput # what the plan says
weeks = scope / throughput                 # what it will take
weeks_late = weeks - planned_weeks         # the delay the growth alone adds

# Result
planned_weeks
weeks
weeks_late
P(weeks > deadline)               # how likely are we to miss the date?
